sometimes even the most powerful  filmmakers in hollywood  take the long way to getting their  visions on screen  from the involvement of a legendary  filmmaker to the future of the franchise  here's the untold truth of elita battle  angel  though elita battle angel premiered in  theaters in february 2019  james cameron had been developing the  project for quite a while  in fact cameron was pursuing elita all  the way at the dawn of the 21st century  back in june 2000 news sprung up that  20th century fox  had registered a website domain related  to elita for cameron  at the time fox had no comment on what  specific plans they had for this webpage  coming less than three years after  cameron's titanic had dominated the  planet  though grabbing that sight couldn't help  but draw eyeballs  it seemed to be news that positioned  elita as the next directorial effort  from the king of the world  as history is proven though all that  speculation  around 2000 never led to much though he  went back and forth on which project to  do  as his next directorial effort cameron  eventually shifted his sights onto  avatar  his connection to elita would be further  distanced once the director's chair was  filled by robert rodriguez  still cameron remained an integral  creative partner on the project  the fact that he was pursuing this  endeavor all the way back in 2000  speaks to his enduring passion for the  world of elita  as the 21st century began cameron always  wanted to push the envelope for visual  effects  was looking to make movies starring  entirely digital characters  both elita and avatar were being  eyeballed by the attur  as ways of realizing those ambitions  with the former  initially being the one cameron planned  to make into a groundbreaking reality  first  all the way back in 2004 cameron was  teasing the movie  which he dubbed battle angel as a  project featuring a main character done  entirely in cg  animation which would be shot with a new  3d imaging system he'd developed for  documentaries  cameron's visual effects ambitions for  the project were clear from the get-go  while his explicit mention of battle  angel being in pre-production  made it obvious he planned to get to the  film next  however plans eventually changed cameron  debated whether he'd direct avatar or  battle angel next  but camera tests eventually led him to  pursue the former instead in the process  alita went from being a top priority to  getting shifted to cameron's back burner  it can take a while for a movie's visual  effects work to come together just right  that's why a number of blockbusters  begin working on their most vfx heavy  sequences before principal photography  even begins in the case of elita battle  angel it shouldn't be shocking to  discover that the cutting edge  technology  used to bring those robotic characters  to life was being worked on  long before cameras started rolling  however what is surprising  is just how long this vfx technology was  being fine-tuned  elita battle angels vfx were being  worked on for more than a decade  before it ever hit the silver screen  according to a may  2006 profile from variety james cameron  had spent about 10 months at that point  working on the visual effects technology  necessary to bring the movie to life  cameron even at these earliest stages  planned to render elita the character as  an entirely digital creation  so he wanted to make sure the technology  used for this protagonist was just right  of course cameron's early prep work  didn't pan out as he focused his  attention  on jake sully and his adventures on  pandora  still having elita's vfx date all the  way back to 2005  reflects cameron's determination to  render this anime character right  in live action robert rodriguez doesn't  frequently play in the sandbox of big  budget movies  he certainly made vfx heavy features but  budgets on the scale of a james cameron  mega blockbuster  aren't exactly rodriguez's wheelhouse  though he embraced  this style of filmmaking when he took on  elita battle angel  rodriguez's original participation in  the production was meant to be quite a  bit more limited  initially rodriguez was simply called in  to help revise the film's screenplay but  he grew more invested when he saw the  design work  at play as he explained to the irish  times i saw james cameron's original  drawings  and they took my breath away and he  trusted me with the version  that was in his head and he said if you  fix the script for me  you can direct so a month later i come  back and say  here you go free of charge and he said  all right  it's yours after that rodriguez went  from being a screenwriter on elita  battle angel to being its sole director  i said if you can crack the code and you  want to do it  let's do it elita actress rosa salazar  became one of the most acclaimed parts  of elita battle angel  with critics praising how she was able  to convey a richly human  performance through all that motion  capture animation technology  however despite how widely beloved  salazar's elita has become  she wasn't always the only person in  contention for the role  originally the title role of velita  battle angel came down to a number of  actresses  including future spider-man mainstay  zendaya the hollywood reporter noted in  april 2016  that zendaya salazar and it follows lead  micah monroe  were all finalists for the role of elita  bella thorne was also mentioned as a  name and consideration for the part  interestingly at the time thr said that  zendaya was the front-runner for the  role  but cautioned that the performer's  commitments to her disney channel  program  kc undercover could provide  insurmountable scheduling conflicts  it turned out those conflicts were  impossible to resolve  and zendaya failed to secure the role of  elita while other contenders like monroe  and thorne  also fell by the wayside instead salazar  took on the part forever altering her  career in the process  i do not stand by in the presence of  evil  robert rodriguez needed to make a number  of changes to his filmmaking style when  tackling elita battle angel  the man famous for handling all behind  the scenes elements of his independent  productions had to hand over the reins  of cinematography  music and editing to other people  meanwhile the sheer scope of the entire  endeavor  meant he had to pull back on some of his  most outlandish tendencies  one thing that didn't change though was  that elita was shot  in rodriguez's go-to filming location of  austin texas  the home of rodriguez's troublemaker  studios elita shot on soundstages in the  city  with apparently the entire feature being  filmed there this makes it a rare  big-budget production to shoot in texas  many blockbusters opt to shoot elsewhere  thanks to tax incentives  however those concerns weren't going to  show away rodriguez  in fact he's got a sense of loyalty  fueling his ambitions  to shoot his film in this famous texas  city  as he told the irish times richard  linklater and i both live there and i  have to say  by staying in your community and making  your movies there  and using local workers it creates a  ripple effect that is ultimately  huge with that kind of potential  positive impact it's no wonder  that elita battle angel and its backdrop  of iron city found a home  in the lone star state elita battle  angel  did okay but not necessarily fantastic  at the worldwide box office thanks to a  lack of new american blockbusters in the  first two months of 2019  it managed to do significantly better  domestically than many other live-action  anime adaptations but it still grossed  just over 85 million dollars  domestically  thanks to overseas grosses including a  strong gross in china  alita brought its worldwide box office  hall to 401.9 million dollars  that isn't spectacular on a budget  that's been speculated to range from 170  million dollars to a whopping 200  million dollar range  however it's a decent gross on a number  of levels particularly when you compare  its domestic haul  to its international one while it might  not have done james cameron blockbuster  numbers  elena was also notable because it became  robert rodriguez's biggest movie ever  at the worldwide box office the film  easily leaped past rodriguez's previous  biggest movie ever  the first spy kids film with almost  double the box office total  of course this isn't exactly a shocking  development giving that rodriguez hadn't  previously dabbled in the kinds of  movies that make  over 400 million dollars worldwide when  many of your features are low budget  grind house homages  like machete of course a broadly  appealing tentpole like elita  will become your highest grossing  directorial effort however  it's still a noteworthy achievement for  elita battle angel  especially considering that its box  office run as a whole  didn't quite meet expectations  throughout elita battle angel a handful  of big name actors  show up for brief appearances jai  courtney  pops up as legendary motorball player  joshu gunn  and edward norton appears as the film's  ultimate villain  nova in the moment they're just further  evidence of the larger world that elita  occupies  in the broader context though these  characters and their respective  performers were all supposed to pay off  in potential follow-ups to elita battle  angel as rodriguez  explained in an interview with coming  soon we had to cast these people without  really having a part for them to be  basing it on  to see if they wanted to do it there was  no script for a future one  so we went to people we knew according  to rodriguez these elita cameos were the  last casting they did on the film  in part because the roles were so small  there wasn't a lot of preparation  necessary  delaying the casting also meant  rodriguez and company could really feel  out  who was right for the roles just in case  they didn't get the chance to come back  for sequels  while the future of elita battle angel  as an ongoing cinematic universe is  uncertain  if any sequels do emerge the first movie  has ensured that a handful of big actors  are ready to fill out critical  characters  nobody involved with elita battle angel  could have ever predicted the film would  occupy a notable place in film history  however that's just what happened when  the film was released in the middle  of february 2019 it may have been just a  spot on the calendar at one point but at  the time this meant the film was the  last title released by 20th century fox  before the studio was absorbed into  disney  in march 2019 that's right nearly 85  years of 20th century fox existing  as a non-disney entity came to a close  with leda  though there could never be a perfect  closing film for a studio that  encompassed  so many eras of history concluding on  alita meant that fox went out with a  feature  hailing from one of its biggest go-to  filmmakers  james cameron after all the man behind  fox's two biggest movies at the  worldwide box office  avatar and titanic was also the producer  and screenwriter behind the studio's  final pre-disney release it also meant  that fox went out with a big budget  temple  rather than a smaller scale title that  could have slipped through the pop  culture cracks  initially elite battle angel was meant  to spawn further adventures  and director robert rodriguez noted that  his experience writing the film  meant that he had a clear perspective on  how the character could continue in  future installments  as he explained to yahoo movies whether  you have a franchise  or not you have a character that's so  rich that the audience can imagine more  movies with  those are the kinds of characters that i  like unfortunately  the film's worldwide box office was  nowhere near big enough to immediately  trigger  a green light for such projects despite  those issues though  rodriguez hasn't given up on seeing  further elite adventures  as recently as january 2021 the director  said  that a follow-up could emerge thanks to  the power of streaming services  as he told forbes i think anything is  possible disney bought fox  and they have disney plus so that is  worth the conversation  i know other people would love to see  another and i would love to do another  one  no further updates have emerged so it's  unclear if this is just wishful thinking  on the part of rodriguez  but with the avenue of streaming  services elita fans  may still have a whisper of hope of  seeing further adventures  in iron city check out one of our newest  videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one  [Music]  you

